(PREFACE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As a picture of the manners and customs of the Vagabond population of) Tj T*
(Central Europe before the Reformation, I think this little book, the) Tj T*
(earliest of its kind, will be found interesting. The fact of Luther) Tj T*
(writing a Preface and editing it gives it at once some degree of) Tj T*
(importance, and excites the curiosity of the student.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In this country the _Liber Vagatorum_ is almost unknown, and in Germany) Tj T*
(only a few scholars and antiquaries are acquainted with the book.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In translating it I have endeavoured as much as possible to preserve) Tj T*
(the spirit and peculiarities of the original. Some may object to the) Tj T*
(style as being too antique; but this garb I thought preserved a small) Tj T*
(portion of the original quaintness, and was best suited to the period) Tj T*
ET
endstream
