(children, who are known in the town or village wherein they beg, and) Tj T*
(who would, I doubt not, leave off begging if they could only thrive) Tj T*
(by their handicraft or other honest means, for there is many a godly) Tj T*
(man who begs unwillingly, and feels ashamed before those who knew him) Tj T*
(formerly when he was better off, and before he was compelled to beg.) Tj T*
(Could he but proceed without he would soon leave begging behind him.) Tj T*
