(chapel,?and they pass themselves off for friars from the same place.) Tj T*
(_Item_, that the chapel was poor and they beg linen-thread for an) Tj T*
(altar-cloth \(_id est_, a gown [CLAFFOT] for a harlot [SCHREFEN]\).) Tj T*
(_Item_, fragments of silver for a chalice \(_id est_, to spend it in) Tj T*
(drinking [VERSCHÖCHERN] or gambling [VERJONEN]\). _Item_, towels for the) Tj T*
(priests to dry their hands upon, \(_id est_, to sell [VERKÜMMERN] them\).) Tj T*
(_Item_, there are also DOBISSERS, church-beggars, who have letters) Tj T*
(with seals, and beg alms to repair a ruined chapel \(DIFTEL\), or to) Tj T*
(build a new church. Verily, such friars _do_ make collections for an) Tj T*
(_edificium_?viz. one which lies not far below the nose, and is called) Tj T*
(St. Drunkard?s chapel.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Conclusio_: As to these DOBISSERS, give them nought, for they cheat) Tj T*
(and defraud thee. If from a church that lies ij or iij miles from thee) Tj T*
(people come and beg, give them as much as thou wilt or canst.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(+Of Kammesierers, or Learned Beggars+.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The vjth chapter is about the KAMMESIERERS. These beggars are) Tj T*
(young scholars or young students, who do not obey their fathers and) Tj T*
(mothers, and do not listen to their masters? teaching, and so depart,) Tj T*
(and fall into the bad company of such as are learned in the arts) Tj T*
(of strolling and tramping, and who quickly help them to lose all) Tj T*
(they have by gambling \(VERJONEN\), pawning \(VERSENKEN\), or selling) Tj T*
(\(VERKÜMMERN\) it, with drinking \(VERSCHÖCHERN\) and revelry. And when) Tj T*
(they have nought more left, they learn begging, and KAMMESIERING, and) Tj T*
(to cheat the farmers \(HANZEN-BESEFLEN\); and they KAMESIER as) Tj T*
(follows: _Item_, that they come from Rome \(_id est_, from the brothel) Tj T*
([SONNENBOSS]\), studying to become priests \(on the gallows, _i.e._) Tj T*
(DOLMAN\); _item_, one is _acolitus_, another is _epistolarius_,) Tj T*
(the third _evangelicus_, and a fourth _clericus_ \(GALCH\); _item_, they) Tj T*
(have nought on earth but the alms wherewith people help them, and all) Tj T*
(their friends and family have long been called away by death?s song.) Tj T*
(_Item_, they ask linen cloth for an alb \(_id est_, for a harlot?s) Tj T*
(shift, _i.e._ GLIDEN HANFSTAUDEN\). _Item_, money, that they may be) Tj T*
(consecrated at next Corpus Christi day \(_id est_, in a SONNENBOSS,) Tj T*
(_i.e._ brothel\), and whatever they get by cheating and begging they) Tj T*
(lose in gambling \(VERJONEN\), or with strumpets, or spend it in drink) Tj T*
(\(VERSCHOCHERNS und VERBOLENS\). _Item_, they shave tonsures) Tj T*
(on their heads, although they are not ordained and have no church) Tj T*
(document \(FORMAT\), though they say they have, and they are altogether a) Tj T*
(bad lot \(LOE VOT\).) Tj T*
